WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.661
- And also these snacks
really easy to eat on the go.

00:00:02.661 --> 00:00:04.350
(chewing)

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:05.570
I don't know where I'm going.

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:06.710
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:09.440
So today we're gonna be talking
about what I eat in a day.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:10.720
I've seen a lot of your comments,

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:11.950
I've seen how excited

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:13.770
and interested you are about nutrition.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:16.120
I'm gonna be showing you
exactly what I ate yesterday.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.510
Most of it's not home cooked,

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:19.700
it's not fancy, but it is nutritious

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.490
and it's food that I genuinely enjoy.

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:23.330
It's time for me to go into the hospital.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:25.820
It's gonna be a crazy day
'cause I'm starting super early

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:27.280
and I have a really late day

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.350
but when it's a gorgeous day like this,

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:31.370
it definitely makes it a lot easier.

00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:34.633
So for breakfast today, I'm
doing one of my favorites,

00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:38.010
avocado toast with a little smoked salmon.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:40.095
Get your essential fatty acids in.

00:00:40.095 --> 00:00:42.178
(grunts)

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.644
So good.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:45.515
Look at that.

00:00:45.515 --> 00:00:46.556
You want a bite?

00:00:46.556 --> 00:00:47.700
You want a bite?

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:48.950
No, it's for me.

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:50.627
Breakfast.

00:00:50.627 --> 00:00:52.360
(hip hop music)

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:53.940
It's known as the most important meal

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.840
of the day but not everybody wakes up

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.270
with an appetite so I understand

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:58.490
if breakfast isn't for everyone

00:00:58.490 --> 00:00:59.470
but if you do eat breakfast,

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:00.800
you're getting a lot of health benefits

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:01.860
throughout the day.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:03.780
Not only do you kickstart your metabolism

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.210
which allows you to burn
calories throughout the day,

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.840
but you're also giving
yourself enough energy

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:08.680
to get to the gym.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:11.340
First ingredient very
simple whole wheat bread.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.050
I really enjoy whole wheat
bread versus white bread.

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.500
Whole wheat bread contains
complex carbohydrates

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.930
versus simple carbohydrates
that you find in white bread.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:20.380
What it does is it give you energy

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.080
to be utilized throughout the day

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:23.880
instead of just giving you one quick peak

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.170
and then a crash later on,

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:26.970
and sometimes get into that hangry state

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:27.803
that we all know about.

00:01:27.803 --> 00:01:29.220
- Ma, the meatloaf!

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:30.760
- Next, light cream cheese.

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:33.490
You need saturated fat to
make hormones in your body,

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:35.240
and while it does raise bad cholesterol,

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:36.850
it also raises good cholesterol.

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:39.800
Next ingredient, my favorite
ingredient, avocados.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:42.440
Avocado is actually the
Aztec word for testicle

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:44.090
because avocados do hang in pairs

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:45.890
with one hanging lower than the other

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:47.140
so they do resemble testicles.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.030
Pretty cool fact.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:50.190
They contain a lot of antioxidants

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:51.410
and they're rich in fiber.

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:53.400
Yes, avocado does contain a lot of fat,

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:56.040
but it's important to remember
that it's unsaturated fat

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:58.360
and that unsaturated fat actually helps

00:01:58.360 --> 00:01:59.830
increase your good cholesterol,

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:01.760
and does not affect your bad cholesterol.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:03.050
Lastly, we have salmon.

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:04.760
It's a great ingredient
to add to you meals

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:07.950
because it contains proteins,
omega 3's, antioxidants,

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:10.623
and on top of everything
else, it's delicious.

00:02:12.096 --> 00:02:13.000
(chime)

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.033
It's snack time.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.730
I just finished rounds, I
have to go to research day.

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:19.829
Need a snack, lunch is still
a good three hours away.

00:02:19.829 --> 00:02:21.670
I really like the Perfect Bar

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:24.630
because it's made of
good quality ingredients.

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:26.060
I'm not their spokesperson,

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:27.560
but I'm definitely a big fan.

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:28.870
They contain a lot of protein,

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:30.810
they're made with good
quality ingredients,

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:32.500
and because they have to be refrigerated,

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:34.500
you know there's no preservatives.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:37.060
It's lunch time, just got my favorite meal

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:39.740
for lunch right here, a
little Chipotle action.

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:41.220
I'm eating with my colleagues here,

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:42.910
say hello colleagues.

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:43.743
They said hi.

00:02:43.743 --> 00:02:45.440
While some doctors go to the cafeteria,

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:47.510
if I'm not on call I like
to get out of the hospital

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:50.410
for a bit, so I do run out to Chipotle.

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:52.460
It's one of my favorite
places to get lunch.

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:54.290
I really like the
ingredients that they use.

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:55.690
I think they're really tasty,

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:57.529
and what I really enjoy
is that you're in control,

00:02:57.529 --> 00:03:00.120
you get to chose what
ingredients go into your plate.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:01.660
I really like to get a burrito bowl

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:04.000
instead of a burrito or a quesadilla

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.420
because it avoids some of
the extra carbohydrates

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:07.530
that you get from getting a wrap,

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:08.820
but the things that I do like to make

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.790
is to get a burrito bowl
with either chicken or steak,

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.160
both high in protein.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:15.350
There's been a lot said
about eating red meat,

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:16.780
it increases risk of cancer,

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:18.905
and while that's true in high amounts,

00:03:18.905 --> 00:03:21.641
if you eat it in moderate
amounts in a good balance,

00:03:21.641 --> 00:03:23.140
it's obviously not a problem.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:26.300
We have black beans, they are zero fat,

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.960
and they're one of the
richest foods in fiber

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:30.610
which actually allows you to decrease

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.063
some of the bad cholesterol
that you can get

00:03:32.063 --> 00:03:33.810
through eating an unhealthy diet.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:34.740
Brown rice.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:37.020
Brown rice is definitely
superior to white rice.

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:38.670
It's a complex carbohydrate,

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:41.150
it doesn't peak your sugar
level like white rice does.

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:42.850
Next I like to go for guacamole.

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:44.450
They always say, "Do you
know that it's extra?"

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.730
And I always say, "Yeah
I do, but well worth it."

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:48.470
I get the mild salsa because I'm not a fan

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:50.170
of my food being too spicy.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:53.340
Last but not least, I love cheese.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:54.750
It gives you a little bit of calcium,

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:55.940
a little bit of vitamin D.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:57.530
Overall, this is a nutritious meal

00:03:57.530 --> 00:03:58.950
for someone that shares my goals

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:01.140
of trying to keep weight
on and build muscle.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.180
You have a good mix of
complex carbohydrates,

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:07.240
proteins, vitamins, fiber,
all great nutrients,

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:09.300
but it's important to
know that these meals

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:11.410
do contain a lot of sodium.

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:13.130
Chipotle's known for
that and now they started

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:15.340
putting their sodium content on the menus,

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:17.700
so keep that in mind because excess sodium

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:20.160
can put extra pressure on
your heart and kidneys.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:21.880
I am an athlete and the rest of my day

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:23.145
I don't take in much sodium,

00:04:23.145 --> 00:04:25.390
so I think it's a great meal for me,

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:26.840
but just again, keep that in mind

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:29.770
that the sodium content
in this meal is high.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:33.044
(dramatic music)

00:04:33.044 --> 00:04:34.350
You know what time it is?

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:36.312
It's snack time, again.

00:04:36.312 --> 00:04:39.010
Got my carrots and nuts.

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:40.320
Perfect healthy snack.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:42.400
What's beautiful about
these almonds right here

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.610
is that they contain vitamin E, fiber,

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:46.754
they keep your hair and
nails looking fresh.

00:04:46.754 --> 00:04:50.830
The carrots, you know I love carrots.

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:53.980
Carrots are rich in vitamin
A, known as beta-keratin.

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:57.140
Almonds, great, unsaturated
fats, vitamin E.

00:04:57.140 --> 00:05:00.120
Great food to eat for healthy
hair, nails, and skin,

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:02.520
and in general, I think
that they're fun to eat.

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:08.564
Oh!

00:05:08.564 --> 00:05:11.147
(upbeat music)

00:05:12.126 --> 00:05:13.410
- Is there a doctor in the house?

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:16.790
- Just ordered some sushi,
crazy day in the hospital,

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:18.480
but gotta get my protein in,

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:20.560
gotta get my omega-3 fatty acids.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:22.100
I like to get a variety of sushi

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:23.670
and I get the real sushi.

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:26.620
Not the sushi that people eat
with the rolls and all that.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:30.130
Just fish on top of
brown rice, very clean.

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:31.878
It's really my favorite
meal to end the day,

00:05:31.878 --> 00:05:34.270
get ready for the next
day without overeating

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:36.210
and feeling fully
stuffed when I go to bed.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:39.060
This is my go to dinner meal.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:41.990
I love fish, I love the
omega-3s that they provide.

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:43.970
There's not a lot of calories in here.

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:45.830
I prefer eating my sushi with brown rice,

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:47.620
we talked about the benefits earlier.

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:50.070
You get complex carbohydrates,
you get proteins,

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:52.430
it's a clean meal, it fills you up,

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:54.360
and really, it does taste great.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:56.340
Important to note about fish,

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:58.130
wild fish is better than farm fish

00:05:58.130 --> 00:06:00.160
because it contains less mercury.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:01.540
There's a lot of news going around

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:03.420
about how mercury poisoning is bad,

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:05.110
so if you are eating farm fish,

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:07.530
make sure no more than three
to four servings a week.

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:09.680
So that's what I actually eat in a day

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:11.230
and it's not something
that I eat every day.

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:13.660
I know yesterday I consumed
probably more sodium

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:16.000
than I should have, but
in general, it's balanced,

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.760
it's in moderation, and that's
really the smart way to go.

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:20.840
This diet obviously does
not work for everybody

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:22.390
and I don't recommend it for everybody.

00:06:22.390 --> 00:06:23.770
If you're interested in the calories

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:26.020
